WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:03.300
- When I was a freshman in
college I made a ton of money

00:00:03.300 --> 00:00:04.920
in what I can only describe

00:00:04.920 --> 00:00:07.050
as the weirdest of circumstances.

00:00:07.050 --> 00:00:08.343
And this is that story.

00:00:08.900 --> 00:00:09.733
Hello again.

00:00:09.733 --> 00:00:11.800
Before we dive in, I should emphasize

00:00:11.800 --> 00:00:13.370
how weird this story is.

00:00:13.370 --> 00:00:14.610
It doesn't make any sense.

00:00:14.610 --> 00:00:16.430
But, it's completely true.

00:00:16.430 --> 00:00:19.210
I'm also gonna be vague
about names, locations,

00:00:19.210 --> 00:00:21.893
specifics because you'll see.

00:00:22.690 --> 00:00:23.523
Here we go.

00:00:23.523 --> 00:00:27.180
So I was 19, a freshman
in college, a.k.a broke.

00:00:27.180 --> 00:00:29.100
So one day I'm just hanging
out with some friends

00:00:29.100 --> 00:00:30.870
and someone mentions that there's,

00:00:30.870 --> 00:00:31.980
I don't know what else to call it,

00:00:31.980 --> 00:00:34.963
but an event happening where
students could make money.

00:00:34.970 --> 00:00:36.813
Oh cool, what do we have to do?

00:00:36.840 --> 00:00:37.920
Tutor some kids?

00:00:37.920 --> 00:00:39.120
Hand out some flyers?

00:00:39.120 --> 00:00:39.953
What are we talking here?

00:00:39.953 --> 00:00:41.297
"No." he says.

00:00:41.297 --> 00:00:42.377
"There's this bar.

00:00:42.377 --> 00:00:44.413
"You bring your ID with you,

00:00:44.437 --> 00:00:48.917
"show it to these people
and they give you $20.00."

00:00:49.510 --> 00:00:51.130
Just making sure I understand this.

00:00:51.130 --> 00:00:54.023
I show people my license and I get $20.00.

00:00:54.140 --> 00:00:54.973
And that's it.

00:00:55.750 --> 00:00:57.720
Red flag right from the start here.

00:00:57.720 --> 00:00:58.553
What is happening?

00:00:58.553 --> 00:01:01.150
Why would I get money for
just showing someone my ID?

00:01:01.150 --> 00:01:04.833
Of course looking back now,
it sounds incredibly sketchy,

00:01:04.900 --> 00:01:07.390
but then, let's do this.

00:01:07.390 --> 00:01:08.223
Why wouldn't we?

00:01:08.223 --> 00:01:09.210
What's the worst that could happen?

00:01:09.210 --> 00:01:10.840
We don't get $20.00?

00:01:10.840 --> 00:01:11.850
May as well check this out.

00:01:11.850 --> 00:01:14.950
So the day arrives when
this event is happening.

00:01:14.950 --> 00:01:16.507
And a group of us go to this bar,

00:01:16.507 --> 00:01:18.067
"Write down your name and phone number

00:01:18.067 --> 00:01:19.730
"and get in line", someone says.

00:01:19.730 --> 00:01:21.003
Pst, easy.

00:01:21.040 --> 00:01:22.950
Paperwork done, we're waitin' in line,

00:01:22.950 --> 00:01:23.980
we reach the front.

00:01:23.980 --> 00:01:27.210
There's two men behind the
bar, "ID?" the one guy asks.

00:01:27.210 --> 00:01:28.680
20 bucks here we come.

00:01:28.680 --> 00:01:29.963
I hand my license over.

00:01:30.680 --> 00:01:31.697
I can smell the cash.

00:01:31.697 --> 00:01:33.163
"One sec." he says.

00:01:33.410 --> 00:01:35.040
And walks away with my ID.

00:01:35.040 --> 00:01:38.300
Whoa, no, no, no, excuse
me, what is going on,

00:01:38.300 --> 00:01:40.100
this is supposed to be a clean exchange?

00:01:40.100 --> 00:01:41.700
Oh God, I knew this was a bad idea.

00:01:41.700 --> 00:01:42.970
Is my identity stolen?

00:01:42.970 --> 00:01:44.157
I knew this was too good to be,

00:01:44.157 --> 00:01:46.932
"Here", he says and
hands me back my license

00:01:46.932 --> 00:01:48.670
with a 20 dollar bill.

00:01:50.491 --> 00:01:54.523
OK, as for everyone else,
they got $20.00 too.

00:01:54.570 --> 00:01:57.340
So this thing that sounded
completely impossible

00:01:57.530 --> 00:01:59.470
is in fact very real.

00:01:59.470 --> 00:02:01.360
I know what you're thinking, cool story,

00:02:01.360 --> 00:02:02.610
that's a ton of money.

00:02:02.610 --> 00:02:04.150
This story sucks.

00:02:04.150 --> 00:02:06.510
And to that I say, chill,

00:02:06.510 --> 00:02:09.010
because we're just getting started.

00:02:09.010 --> 00:02:11.310
A few days go by and I get a voicemail.

00:02:11.310 --> 00:02:12.400
It was something like,

00:02:12.400 --> 00:02:15.617
"Congratulations, you've been
selected for the next round.

00:02:15.617 --> 00:02:18.040
"Please bring your ID
to the same address."

00:02:18.040 --> 00:02:20.970
What the hell is going on?

00:02:20.970 --> 00:02:23.830
Only one other friend of
mine got this voicemail.

00:02:23.830 --> 00:02:25.650
They were narrowing people down.

00:02:25.650 --> 00:02:28.570
Was I supposed to be excited or terrified.

00:02:28.570 --> 00:02:29.620
I weighed my options.

00:02:29.620 --> 00:02:31.570
My ID was probably being used

00:02:31.570 --> 00:02:34.163
to take out loans for
drug mansions overseas.

00:02:34.487 --> 00:02:35.470
$20.00.

00:02:35.470 --> 00:02:37.530
I'm now a part of the mafia

00:02:37.530 --> 00:02:39.280
and currently being watched by FBI?

00:02:39.657 --> 00:02:40.833
$20.00.

00:02:41.400 --> 00:02:42.790
Let's do this.

00:02:42.790 --> 00:02:44.600
So the day comes, again.

00:02:44.600 --> 00:02:48.160
I go to the bar, fill out
my name, number, again.

00:02:48.160 --> 00:02:49.703
Shorter line this time.

00:02:49.770 --> 00:02:52.070
Apparently these IDs were
the best of the best.

00:02:52.070 --> 00:02:54.700
I get up to the bar, hand my ID over,

00:02:54.700 --> 00:02:56.690
he walks away, again.

00:02:56.690 --> 00:02:58.770
This is probably where
my good luck runs out.

00:02:58.770 --> 00:03:00.810
He'll come back and say I have to apply

00:03:00.810 --> 00:03:02.790
for some fake credit card or something.

00:03:02.790 --> 00:03:04.740
It's a shame because I
was really starting to,

00:03:04.740 --> 00:03:07.350
he hands me my ID and $100.00.

00:03:07.350 --> 00:03:10.120
At this point I am really
struggling to not laugh.

00:03:10.120 --> 00:03:11.610
Not only did I get money,

00:03:11.610 --> 00:03:14.050
I got five times the amount of money.

00:03:14.050 --> 00:03:15.290
Is this my job now?

00:03:15.290 --> 00:03:16.520
Is this how I make a living?

00:03:16.520 --> 00:03:19.300
Folks, step right up and take a look at

00:03:19.300 --> 00:03:21.930
what some might call the finest ID

00:03:21.930 --> 00:03:24.150
in these here United States.

00:03:24.150 --> 00:03:25.650
My friends are waiting outside the bar.

00:03:25.650 --> 00:03:27.530
They're just as confused as I am.

00:03:27.530 --> 00:03:30.170
The money is really
starting to pile up here.

00:03:30.170 --> 00:03:31.470
What if I told you this story

00:03:31.470 --> 00:03:33.770
is about to get 10 times weirder?

00:03:33.770 --> 00:03:38.033
Maybe a week goes by, I get
another mysterious voicemail.

00:03:38.127 --> 00:03:41.647
"Congratulations, you've been
selected as the final person,

00:03:41.647 --> 00:03:44.898
"please meet us on Saturday
morning at this intersection."

00:03:44.898 --> 00:03:46.070
Blah, blah, blah, blah, blah.

00:03:46.070 --> 00:03:48.010
This time it wasn't even an address.

00:03:48.010 --> 00:03:51.150
It was just an area
downtown, but in the morning.

00:03:51.150 --> 00:03:53.440
Well, I had a decision to make.

00:03:53.440 --> 00:03:56.150
Do I continue showing up in strange places

00:03:56.150 --> 00:03:57.160
at the promise of money?

00:03:57.160 --> 00:03:59.030
With no idea what's waiting for me?

00:03:59.030 --> 00:04:01.520
Or do I just quit while I'm ahead?

00:04:01.520 --> 00:04:03.657
As you're watching this,
you're probably like,

00:04:03.657 --> 00:04:06.237
"Brigid, come on, there's no way

00:04:06.237 --> 00:04:07.777
"you're dumb enough to see this through.

00:04:07.777 --> 00:04:10.470
"You probably came to your
senses like a sane human being."

00:04:10.470 --> 00:04:11.910
Let's do this.

00:04:11.910 --> 00:04:14.060
I know, I know, it's bad, okay.

00:04:14.060 --> 00:04:15.053
But I went.

00:04:15.200 --> 00:04:17.450
I wanted to see what
life had in store for me.

00:04:17.450 --> 00:04:18.713
I didn't go alone though.

00:04:18.730 --> 00:04:19.640
I brought a friend.

00:04:19.640 --> 00:04:21.300
We head to this corner downtown.

00:04:21.300 --> 00:04:22.700
We're standing there on the sidewalk.

00:04:22.700 --> 00:04:24.280
What are we supposed to be looking for?

00:04:24.280 --> 00:04:27.550
Suddenly a van door just slides open.

00:04:27.550 --> 00:04:29.500
Yeah, a van.

00:04:29.500 --> 00:04:30.333
This is it.

00:04:30.660 --> 00:04:31.570
This is how I die.

00:04:31.570 --> 00:04:34.120
There's a group of at least
five people in this van.

00:04:34.120 --> 00:04:35.510
A man and a woman get out.

00:04:35.510 --> 00:04:37.207
Goodbye cruel world.

00:04:37.207 --> 00:04:39.170
"Alright, so here's what's gonna happen."

00:04:39.170 --> 00:04:40.677
The woman hands me an envelope.

00:04:40.677 --> 00:04:43.263
"There's $7,000.00 cash in here.

00:04:43.687 --> 00:04:45.060
"And here's a list."

00:04:45.060 --> 00:04:45.893
I'm an assassin.

00:04:45.893 --> 00:04:47.787
I'm an assassin now and
this is my hit list.

00:04:47.787 --> 00:04:49.477
"The games are in order of priority,

00:04:49.477 --> 00:04:51.460
"seats together, no partial viewing."

00:04:51.460 --> 00:04:53.560
I glance around as she's talking.

00:04:53.560 --> 00:04:55.623
Oh, we're outside of the stadium.

00:04:55.780 --> 00:04:56.613
Wait, wait, wait.

00:04:56.613 --> 00:04:59.700
Am I buying tickets to a sporting event?

00:04:59.700 --> 00:05:01.610
If you're thinking of leaving this video,

00:05:01.610 --> 00:05:04.040
don't, because this story gets crazier.

00:05:04.040 --> 00:05:05.470
The lady explains to me

00:05:05.470 --> 00:05:07.960
that I'm about to have
the chance to buy tickets

00:05:07.960 --> 00:05:10.840
that the general public
doesn't have access to yet.

00:05:10.840 --> 00:05:14.210
It was up to me to get as
many of the games on this list

00:05:14.230 --> 00:05:15.063
as possible.

00:05:15.063 --> 00:05:19.630
Okay, okay, a little confusing
with all of the requests

00:05:19.630 --> 00:05:20.463
that they had.

00:05:20.463 --> 00:05:21.947
But this isn't nearly as scary,

00:05:21.947 --> 00:05:24.187
"One more thing", the woman says,

00:05:24.187 --> 00:05:26.970
"Under no circumstances do you tell anyone

00:05:27.047 --> 00:05:29.660
"where you got this money or who we are."

00:05:29.660 --> 00:05:30.673
Wait, what?

00:05:30.880 --> 00:05:31.713
Who?

00:05:31.713 --> 00:05:32.546
Why?

00:05:32.546 --> 00:05:33.379
What?

00:05:33.379 --> 00:05:34.212
Real confidence booster.

00:05:34.212 --> 00:05:35.480
At least my friend can come with me.

00:05:35.480 --> 00:05:37.057
We start to walk towards the stadium.

00:05:37.057 --> 00:05:39.790
"No, he stays here."

00:05:39.790 --> 00:05:42.100
Of course, leaving my
friend on the corner.

00:05:42.100 --> 00:05:43.330
All by myself.

00:05:43.330 --> 00:05:44.170
Here goes nothing.

00:05:44.170 --> 00:05:46.940
There was a small group of
rich looking businessmen

00:05:46.940 --> 00:05:48.420
gathered outside the stadium.

00:05:48.420 --> 00:05:50.141
Someone from inside the stadium

00:05:50.141 --> 00:05:51.807
pokes their head out of the door,

00:05:51.807 --> 00:05:54.240
"We're ready for you, follow me this way."

00:05:54.240 --> 00:05:56.430
I'm assuming that includes me.

00:05:56.430 --> 00:05:58.900
We walk into the stadium, down this hall

00:05:58.900 --> 00:06:01.450
and the guy pushes what looks like a wall.

00:06:01.450 --> 00:06:05.410
It's a door that leads into
this dimly lit conference room.

00:06:05.410 --> 00:06:08.200
There is no one under 35
years old, except for me.

00:06:08.200 --> 00:06:10.800
There are no women in
this room, except for me.

00:06:10.800 --> 00:06:12.660
Everyone is in a suit, except for me.

00:06:12.660 --> 00:06:14.750
The same person who
let us into the stadium

00:06:14.750 --> 00:06:16.840
explains how we'll be picking games

00:06:16.840 --> 00:06:18.380
and who gets what tickets.

00:06:18.380 --> 00:06:22.250
I stuck exactly to what the
people in the van had told me.

00:06:22.250 --> 00:06:23.680
Eventually we were done.

00:06:23.680 --> 00:06:25.327
The stadium person speaks up again,

00:06:25.327 --> 00:06:27.107
"I don't imagine this is the case,

00:06:27.107 --> 00:06:29.547
"but no one is paying with cash correct?"

00:06:29.547 --> 00:06:31.360
My stomach does a back flip.

00:06:31.360 --> 00:06:34.420
All the businessmen are
obviously shaking their heads no.

00:06:34.420 --> 00:06:36.230
Shit, shit, shit, shit.

00:06:36.230 --> 00:06:37.350
I have to raise my hand.

00:06:37.350 --> 00:06:39.770
I literally have an envelope of $7,000.00.

00:06:39.770 --> 00:06:40.603
Yes, I have cash.

00:06:40.603 --> 00:06:43.460
Ahem, um, I am paying with cash.

00:06:43.460 --> 00:06:46.460
Everyone was clearly aware
of the small blonde girl

00:06:46.460 --> 00:06:49.410
from the start, but now
everyone's eyes are on me.

00:06:49.410 --> 00:06:51.787
It felt like I was in a
movie when someone goes,

00:06:51.787 --> 00:06:53.237
- "She doesn't even go here."

00:06:53.800 --> 00:06:55.227
- But that didn't happen.

00:06:55.227 --> 00:06:57.447
"Okay, you can swing around
to the front of the stadium

00:06:57.447 --> 00:06:58.800
"and pick your tickets up there."

00:06:58.800 --> 00:07:00.030
We all go out front.

00:07:00.030 --> 00:07:01.360
Everything seems normal.

00:07:01.360 --> 00:07:02.943
I walk to the ticket window.

00:07:03.060 --> 00:07:05.560
Slide my list of games through the slot.

00:07:05.560 --> 00:07:09.080
The woman behind the glass
looks me, up and down.

00:07:09.080 --> 00:07:11.490
She turns around and
puts all of the tickets

00:07:11.490 --> 00:07:13.200
I need into an envelope.

00:07:13.200 --> 00:07:15.510
She slides it back through
the slot towards me.

00:07:15.510 --> 00:07:17.373
I calmly reach for them,

00:07:17.450 --> 00:07:19.570
but her hand is still on the tickets.

00:07:19.570 --> 00:07:20.800
All sound is gone.

00:07:20.800 --> 00:07:21.960
I feel like I'm gonna throw up.

00:07:21.960 --> 00:07:24.853
With the deepest eye
contact I've ever felt,

00:07:25.020 --> 00:07:28.577
she looks at me and asks, "Who sent you?"

00:07:29.210 --> 00:07:30.363
I stare back at her.

00:07:31.250 --> 00:07:32.203
I say nothing.

00:07:32.260 --> 00:07:34.490
With her other hand the woman turns around

00:07:34.490 --> 00:07:35.460
to pick up a phone.

00:07:35.460 --> 00:07:37.180
I don't know who she wants to call,

00:07:37.180 --> 00:07:39.300
but I don't want to
stick around to find out.

00:07:39.300 --> 00:07:41.030
I slam the cash on the counter.

00:07:41.030 --> 00:07:42.290
I grab the tickets.

00:07:42.290 --> 00:07:43.210
And I run.

00:07:43.210 --> 00:07:44.860
I run as fast as I can.

00:07:44.860 --> 00:07:47.200
Thinking back, I didn't hear anything,

00:07:47.200 --> 00:07:49.130
no yelling, no sirens.

00:07:49.130 --> 00:07:51.140
After all, I did pay for the tickets.

00:07:51.140 --> 00:07:52.940
Not with my money, but I paid for them.

00:07:52.940 --> 00:07:55.680
The air stings my lungs as
I make it back to the van

00:07:55.680 --> 00:07:56.930
out of sight of the stadium.

00:07:56.930 --> 00:07:58.530
My friend is still, unharmed.

00:07:58.530 --> 00:08:01.020
Nobody has any idea what
I just went through.

00:08:01.020 --> 00:08:03.180
I practically throw the
tickets into the van.

00:08:03.180 --> 00:08:04.690
They quick flip through the envelope

00:08:04.690 --> 00:08:06.300
checking the tickets against their list.

00:08:06.300 --> 00:08:07.540
The van people look at me.

00:08:07.540 --> 00:08:09.013
They hand me an envelope.

00:08:09.047 --> 00:08:10.080
"This is for you."

00:08:10.080 --> 00:08:12.760
Oh yeah, I'm getting paid for this.

00:08:12.760 --> 00:08:15.110
With a heavy thud the door slides shut

00:08:15.110 --> 00:08:16.220
and the van drives off.

00:08:16.220 --> 00:08:19.480
That would ultimately
be, the last time I saw

00:08:19.500 --> 00:08:20.890
or even heard from these people.

00:08:20.890 --> 00:08:22.440
My friend and I open the envelope.

00:08:22.440 --> 00:08:24.473
It had $500.00 in it.

00:08:24.480 --> 00:08:27.260
To a college student, I
practically struck the lottery.

00:08:27.260 --> 00:08:29.620
Keep in mind that this was $500.00

00:08:29.720 --> 00:08:31.980
for maybe an hour of my time.

00:08:31.980 --> 00:08:34.340
Did I think someone was gonna
steal my kidneys, kinda.

00:08:34.340 --> 00:08:35.648
Was this whole experience worth it?

00:08:35.648 --> 00:08:36.961
Not really, no.

00:08:36.961 --> 00:08:38.030
And guess what?

00:08:38.030 --> 00:08:40.980
That night we all went out to
celebrate my accomplishments.

00:08:40.980 --> 00:08:42.438
And guess who loses their wallet?

00:08:42.438 --> 00:08:43.748
(ding)

00:08:43.930 --> 00:08:44.790
Really great.

00:08:44.790 --> 00:08:46.900
All that had been for nothing.

00:08:46.900 --> 00:08:50.883
But, in the end, I did come
away with a really great story.

00:08:50.949 --> 00:08:53.366
(soft music)

00:09:00.880 --> 00:09:02.240
- Hey Unsolved is on a new channel.

00:09:02.240 --> 00:09:03.073
And now your part.

00:09:03.073 --> 00:09:03.950
- Subscribe here.

00:09:03.950 --> 00:09:05.063
- That was my part.

